# Words added to the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary by hand, or corrected from it.
# Written for Klattara from common American pronunciations, and under its MIT
# license. An entry here replaces every pronunciation the dictionary has for
# that word, its plural and its possessive.
#
# Each line is a word in lowercase, then its sounds in ARPAbet, as in CMUdict:
# vowels end in 1 for the main stress, 2 for secondary stress and 0 for none,
# and each word has one main stress. A second pronunciation would be written
# word(2). Only add a word that the engine gets wrong. Plurals and possessives
# follow by themselves, as "memes" does from "meme" and "Mozart's" from
# "Mozart", but -ed and -ing forms may need their own lines.

